{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall bring them and plant them.</b> Because he did not include himself in the collective, to say 'You shall bring <i>us</i> and plant <i>us</i>,' he thereby prophesied that he would not enter the land. And what he said, <b>the sanctuary, O Adonai, which Your hands have established</b>, is drawn after <b>the mountain of Your inheritance</b>; and the reading of the verse is: 'the mountain of Your inheritance' — that same one which <b>You have established</b> below — is <b>a sanctuary</b> for Your dwelling above. That is, it corresponds to Your dwelling above, and concerning that upper one he mentioned <b>the sanctuary of YHWH, which Your hands have established</b> — this is the sanctuary above. Therefore you will find in the word <b>תטעמו</b> a major <i>zaqef</i> accent, and the letter qoph (קו\"ף) comes dagesh-ed for the intensity of the holiness, for it is a sanctuary corresponding to the Sanctuary. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: the Temple below corresponds to the Temple above. See how he used the language of action for the one below, but for the one above he did not do so; rather, he said <b>which Your hands have established</b> — an allusion to the ten sefirot, and understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The reference to 'the letter qoph comes dagesh-ed' is textually puzzling: the qoph in the verse shows no dagesh in any standard masoretic text. Translated hyper-literally as written; the difficulty is left unresolved."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:38.232209400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}